From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:21:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: release the cached tag name when the multiplayer game
 shuts down

getTagOrigin and getTagAngles keep the last tag name in
level.cachedTagMat with a counted string reference. Only Com_Quit_f
released it, and G_InitGame clears level with memset on every map
change, so the reference was lost and SL_CheckLeaks failed at quit.

Call GScr_Shutdown from G_ShutdownGame, as singleplayer releases its
cached tag names there.
---
 src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp b/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
index 78b5dbb9..724d34ed 100644
--- a/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
+++ b/src/game_mp/g_main_mp.cpp
@@ -830,6 +830,7 @@ void __cdecl G_ShutdownGame(int32_t freeScripts)
     HudElem_DestroyAll();
     if (Scr_IsSystemActive() && !level.savepersist)
         SV_FreeClientScriptPers();
+    GScr_Shutdown(); // release the cached tag name before G_InitGame clears level
     Scr_ShutdownSystem(1u, level.savepersist == 0);
     if (freeScripts)
     {
